{"name":"Boy Red","hex":"#b3111d","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"boy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Bodo (Central Africa)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male child. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A young man."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boy"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boy","blocks":[{"text":"A boy is a young male human. The term is commonly used for a child or an adolescent. When a male human reaches adulthood, they are usually described as a man."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Smiling_little_boy_of_Laos.jpg/330px-Smiling_little_boy_of_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boy","wikidata":"Q3010"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicio